  "debrief": "Logic outputs are signals, not power: a 74HC pin gives about 20 mA at most. A transistor driver turns that small signal into a big current: 0.43 mA into the base controls 36 mA of LEDs. Every relay, buzzer, motor and LED strip on a microcontroller board is driven this way."
